Assume that all gases are perfect and that data refer to 298 K unless otherwise stated. At $298 \mathrm{~K}$ the standard enthalpy of combustion of sucrose is $-5797 \mathrm{~kJ}$ $\mathrm{mol}^{-1}$ and the standard Gibbs energy of the reaction is $-6333 \mathrm{~kJ} \mathrm{~mol}^{-1}$.
Estimate the additional non-expansion work that may be obtained by raising the temperature to blood temperature, $37^{\circ} \mathrm{C}$.

Options:
(A) 0 kJ mol^{-1}
(B) -25 $\mathrm{kJ} \mathrm{mol}^{-1}$
(C) -10 kJ mol^{-1}
(D) -35 kJ mol^{-1}
(E) -21$\mathrm{kJ} \mathrm{mol}^{-1}$
(F) -28 kJ mol^{-1}
(G) -45 kJ mol^{-1}
(H) -18 kJ mol^{-1}
(I) -30 $\mathrm{kJ} \mathrm{mol}^{-1}$
(J) -15 $\mathrm{kJ} \mathrm{mol}^{-1}$

End your response with a final line of the form "Answer: X". X is the letter of the correct option.

Calculate the electrostatic energy of a system consisting of a point charge q located at the center of a spherical conducting shell of inner radius r_1 and outer radius r_2.

Options:
(A) {1 / (4\pi\epsilon_0)} (q / r^2)
(B) {1 / (4\pi\epsilon_0)} (1/4) q^2 {(1 / r_1) - (1 / r_2)}
(C) {1 / (4\pi\epsilon_0)} (q / r_1) - (q / r_2)
(D) {1 / (4\pi\epsilon_0)} (1/2) q^2 {(1 / r_1) - (1 / r_2)}
(E) {1 / (4\pi\epsilon_0)} (1/2) q^2 {(1 / r^2) - (1 / r_1)}
(F) {1 / (4\pi\epsilon_0)} q^2 {(r_2 - r_1) / (r_1 r_2)}
(G) {1 / (4\pi\epsilon_0)} (q^2 / r_1)
(H) {1 / (4\pi\epsilon_0)} (q^2 / r_2)
(I) {1 / (4\pi\epsilon_0)} (q^2 / r_1) - (q^2 / r_2)
(J) {1 / (4\pi\epsilon_0)} (1/2) q^2 {(1 / r_1) + (1 / r_2)}

End your response with a final line of the form "Answer: X". X is the letter of the correct option.

